<!-- The button, as a person judges it: one scene, a release's page,
     with every kind of button the kit has under the labels a program
     gives them. A stories file of a widget (of="button") is a scene
     file: each story's children are what the canvas draws, at the
     window's width. Hover and focus are live: point at a button, or
     Tab to it. -->
<stories of="button" title="Button">
  <story name="Buttons on a release page" about="Every kind of button and the states it has, with the labels a program gives them: point at one to hover it, Tab to focus it.">
    <stack gap="1">
      <section heading="Actions">
        <text muted wrap>The page's main actions. The primary one is filled with the accent; the rest are plain; a bare one has no fill until it is pointed at.</text>
        <row gap="1">
          <button fill="accent"><icon name="rocket-launch-outline"/>Deploy to production</button>
          <button>Save as draft</button>
          <button><icon name="restart"/>Run the checks again</button>
          <button bare>Cancel</button>
        </row>
      </section>
      <section heading="Unavailable">
        <text muted wrap>The same actions while a deploy runs: each is disabled, and takes neither the pointer nor the keyboard.</text>
        <row gap="1">
          <button fill="accent" disabled><icon name="rocket-launch-outline"/>Deploy to production</button>
          <button disabled>Save as draft</button>
          <button disabled><icon name="restart"/>Run the checks again</button>
          <button bare disabled>Cancel</button>
        </row>
      </section>
      <section heading="Tones">
        <text muted wrap>A button that says what it does by its colour: one that waits for someone, one that destroys, one that confirms.</text>
        <row gap="1">
          <button attention><icon name="account-clock-outline"/>Approve the rollout</button>
          <button tone="error"><icon name="trash-can-outline"/>Delete the release</button>
          <button fill="error">Roll back now</button>
          <button fill="ok">Mark as verified</button>
        </row>
      </section>
      <section heading="Icons">
        <text muted wrap>An icon before the label, after it, or alone with a label for a reader.</text>
        <row gap="1">
          <button><icon name="content-copy"/>Copy the build's link</button>
          <button>Open the logs<icon name="arrow-right"/></button>
          <button label="Download the artifact"><icon name="download"/></button>
          <button label="Close" bare><icon name="close"/></button>
        </row>
      </section>
      <section heading="In a row of a list">
        <text muted wrap>A small button is a line tall, so the row that holds one is as tall as the rows that hold none.</text>
        <list>
          <item gap="1"><text grow>api-gateway</text><text small muted>deployed 4 minutes ago</text></item>
          <item gap="1" selected><text grow>billing-worker</text><text small muted>waiting for approval</text><button small>Approve</button><button small bare>Skip</button></item>
          <item gap="1"><text grow>search-indexer</text><text small muted>failed at step 3 of 5</text><button small fill="accent">Retry</button></item>
        </list>
      </section>
      <section heading="On a bar">
        <text muted wrap>Pills: a bar's tools, with no fill at rest. One is raised (a picker), one is current (its tool holds the keyboard), and a badge counts what is new.</text>
        <row gap="1">
          <button pill raised>production<icon name="menu-down"/></button>
          <button pill current><icon name="source-branch"/>main</button>
          <button pill label="Failed checks" badge="3" badge-tone="error"><icon name="flask-outline"/></button>
          <button pill label="Notices" badge-dot><icon name="bell-outline"/></button>
          <button pill label="Settings"><icon name="cog-outline"/></button>
        </row>
      </section>
      <section heading="As one control">
        <text muted wrap>Buttons in a segmented row are one pick of a few; in a row of chips, several are picked at once.</text>
        <row gap="2">
          <row segmented>
            <button selected>All</button>
            <button>Failed</button>
            <button>Running</button>
          </row>
          <row chips gap="1">
            <button selected>production</button>
            <button selected>staging</button>
            <button>preview</button>
          </row>
        </row>
      </section>
    </stack>
  </story>
</stories>
